{
  "schema": 1,
  "scenario": "lsp-typing-off",
  "definitions": {
    "completion": "in the webview: from inserting `.` (the server's trigger character, `view.dispatch` with `input.type`) to the animation frame after the autocomplete popup showed the server's first item; 20 per run; per-run value = median",
    "definition": "answer → frame: from the fake server's stamp just before it wrote the `textDocument/definition` answer (a different file each time, so opening it is included) to the wall clock of the frame after that file's editor showed the cursor on the target line; `gotoDeclaration` (⌘B's function) is called directly — keymap handling is not included; 10 per run; per-run value = median",
    "diagnostics": "publish → frame: from the fake server's stamp just before it wrote the `publishDiagnostics` that marks the edited line to the wall clock of the frame after that line's underline (`.pw-diagnostic`) appeared; 20 per run; per-run value = median. edit → frame (reference) also holds the client's `didChange`",
    "idle": "`lsp-idle`: this repository's copy registered trusted with the real server at `--lsp-server`; after the file opened and the server stayed ready for 15 s, wait idle_secs and sample phys_footprint; Pitwall's processes (`pitwall` and WebKit) and the server's (every other process of the instance) are reported apart",
    "memory": "phys_footprint by the responsible-pid group, sampled after the scenario (symbols: after the popups — the Rust index lives in the `pitwall` process)",
    "problems": "opening `src/problems.rs` makes the fake server publish 5 diagnostics to each of 2,000 files (10,000); after the status bar counts are complete: ⌘6 keydown → the frame after the first problem row; then fling top to bottom in 1500 frames, judged as 06 「스크롤 60fps」 (share within one refresh ≥ 0.95 and median interval ≤ 17 ms)",
    "server": "a fake language server (`pw-perf-lsp`) plugged into the bundled `rust-analyzer` definition by the global setting `[lsp.rust-analyzer] path`; it answers at once and stamps the wall clock of what it sent (the targets are Pitwall's side only, M4-D19)",
    "symbols": "a synthetic repository of 20,000 files and 500,000 symbols registered untrusted (no language server); first index = launch → `index.status` ready with nothing pending (polled every 50 ms on a connection of the same project); then, with no wait, the first popup (⌘⌥O for `symbols`, ⌘O for `classes`) and the query typed a character at a time: input event → the frame after that query's rows were in the DOM (`totalMs`), of which `index.symbols.search` round trip (`rpcMs`, Host + IPC); the second popup is measured the same way afterwards (not a first use)",
    "typing": "300 characters at 50 ms, each inserted with `view.dispatch` (`input.type`, keymap · IME not included); per key: insert → after the next frame's rendering (a message posted from the next animation frame); per-run value = p95. LSP on and off are separate runs (`lsp-typing` · `lsp-typing-off`, the latter with `[lsp.rust-analyzer] enabled = false`); 06 judges on − off ≤ 2 ms on the medians of the per-run p95"
  },
